    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the membership-level 4 tenure rule with minimal structural impact.\n\n**Behaviour:** Level 4 now requires tenure of more than 365 days (registration date to today). A new owner has zero tenure, so it never contributes the +1, keeping a new owner with an email and `namesakeCount == 0` at level 3 \u2014 exactly what `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` asserts.\n\n**Changes (kept small and cohesive):**\n\n1. `OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice.java` \u2014 one edited line in `addNamesakeCount` (raised the cap to 4 and added a `+ tenureLevel(owner)` term), plus a new self-contained 3-line helper `tenureLevel(...)`. All the new decision logic lives in the tiny helper (CC 2), so the existing method's complexity doesn't grow.\n\n2. `openapi.yml` \u2014 updated the `membershipLevel` schema (`maximum: 4` and its description) so the documented contract and the generated `@Max` bean-validation constraint stay consistent with the new cap.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, 1 run / 0 failures.",
